WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.545
NIST SP 800-82 Revision 3 provides practical guidance for operational technology security.

00:00:05.545 --> 00:00:11.444
It broadens the discussion beyond traditional industrial control systems while keeping physical process,

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:15.981
safety, reliability, and availability at the center of security decisions.

00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:20.065
Effective programs understand their assets, topology, communication, dependencies, threats,

00:00:20.065 --> 00:00:21.880
vulnerabilities, and operational consequences.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.871
Risk management connects that evidence to accountable decisions about architecture, controls,

00:00:26.871 --> 00:00:29.140
remediation, residual risk, and recovery.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.224
Defense in depth combines physical protection, segmentation, access control,

00:00:33.224 --> 00:00:37.761
secure remote access, monitoring, vulnerability management, backups, and incident response.

00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:41.845
Architecture should prevent unnecessary direct access and provide controlled,

00:00:41.845 --> 00:00:45.021
observable paths between enterprise and operational functions.

00:00:45.021 --> 00:00:47.290
Security must also be maintained.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:51.374
Inventory, configuration baselines, change control, patch planning, logging, training,

00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:52.024
exercises,

00:00:52.024 --> 00:00:57.015
and lifecycle management keep controls effective as technology and operations evolve.

00:00:57.015 --> 00:01:02.006
Evidence should demonstrate that controls work without creating unacceptable process risk.

00:01:02.006 --> 00:01:06.544
The publication guides decisions but does not replace site-specific judgment.

00:01:06.544 --> 00:01:09.720
Cybersecurity professionals, engineers, operators, safety teams, vendors,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.535
and leadership must collaborate.

00:01:11.535 --> 00:01:15.165
The strongest outcome is not a completed checklist;

00:01:15.165 --> 00:01:20.156
it is a resilient operation that can prevent, detect, respond to,

00:01:20.156 --> 00:01:25.601
and recover from cyber events while continuing to protect people, mission, equipment,

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.220
and the physical process.
